    "q-148673": {
      "dom_id": "step-q148673",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Arthur and Sara are finding the best recipe for chocolate muffins, and they test three different oven cooking modes, mode $1,$ mode $2,$ and mode $3.$ They also try two types of yeast, A and B.\n\n- They use mode $1$ to cook the $30%$ of their muffins, and $90%$ of those muffins turn out well.\n\n- They use mode $2$ to cook the $40%$ of their muffins, and $85%$ of those muffins turn out well.\n\n- They use mode $3$ to cook the $30%$ of their muffins, and $88%$ of those muffins turn out well.\n\nIf $20%$ of all muffins was prepared with yeast A, and $87%$ of yeast A muffins turn out well, what is the probability that a randomly chosen good muffin is done with yeast A? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "Let $A$ be the event that a muffin is made with yeast A, $G$ be the event that a muffin turns out well, and ${M}_{1},{M}_{2},{M}_{3}$ be the event that a muffin is cooked with mode $1,$ $2,$ or $3,$ respectively. \n\nLet's break down the information given in the problem statement:\n\n- From the bullet points, we have the following information:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & P({M}_{1})=0.3 &  & P(G|{M}_{1})=0.9 \\\\  & P({M}_{2})=0.4 &  & P(G|{M}_{2})=0.85 \\\\  & P({M}_{3})=0.3 &  & P(G|{M}_{3})=0.88\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe disjoint union ${M}_{1}⊔{M}_{2}⊔{M}_{3}$ covers the entire sample space, and we have\n\n$$\nP({M}_{1})+P({M}_{2})+P({M}_{3})=0.3+0.4+0.3=1.\n$$\n\n- Since $20%$ of muffins are made with yeast A, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.2.\n$$\n\n- Since $87%$ of muffins made with yeast A turn out well, we have\n\n$$\nP(G|A)=0.87.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that a randomly chosen good muffin is made with yeast A, which is represented as $P(A|G).$ \n\nUsing Bayes' theorem combined with the law of total probability, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A|G) & =\\frac{P(G|A)P(A)}{P(G)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(G|A)P(A)}{P(G|{M}_{1})P({M}_{1})+P(G|{M}_{2})P({M}_{2})+P(G|{M}_{3})P({M}_{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.87)(0.2)}{(0.9)(0.3)+(0.85)(0.4)+(0.88)(0.3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.174}{0.874} \\\\  & ≈0.199,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
