      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "In a nature park, there are $4$ species of squirrels, each with the same population.\n\n- Among the squirrels of species $1,$ $12%$ are born in captivity.\n\n- Among the squirrels of species $2,$ $5%$ are born in captivity.\n\n- Among the squirrels of species $3,$ $6%$ are born in captivity.\n\n- Among the squirrels of species $4,$ $3%$ are born in captivity.\n\nIf $35%$ of the squirrels are adult females, and $8%$ of the adult female squirrels are born in captivity, what is the probability that a randomly chosen squirrel born in captivity is an adult female? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "Let $F$ be the event that a squirrel is an adult female, $C$ be the event that a squirrel is born in captivity, and ${S}_{1},{S}_{2},{S}_{3},{S}_{4}$ be the event that a squirrel is of species $1,$ $2,$ $3,$ or $4,$ respectively. \n\nLet's break down the information given in the problem statement:\n\n- Each species has the same number of squirrels, so we have the following information:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({S}_{1})=P({S}_{2})=P({S}_{3})=P({S}_{4})=0.25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- From the bullet points, we have the following information:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & P(C|{S}_{1})=0.12 \\\\  & P(C|{S}_{2})=0.05 \\\\  & P(C|{S}_{3})=0.06 \\\\  & P(C|{S}_{4})=0.03\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe disjoint union ${S}_{1}⊔{S}_{2}⊔{S}_{3}⊔{S}_{4}$ covers the entire sample space, and we have\n\n$$\nP({S}_{1})+P({S}_{2})+P({S}_{3})+P({S}_{4})=0.25+0.25+0.25+0.25=1.\n$$\n\n- Since $35%$ of the squirrels are adult females, we have\n\n$$\nP(F)=0.35.\n$$\n\n- Since $8%$ of adult females are born in captivity, we have\n\n$$\nP(C|F)=0.08.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that a randomly chosen squirrel born in captivity is an adult female, which is represented as $P(F|C).$ \n\nUsing Bayes' theorem combined with the law of total probability, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(F|C) & =\\frac{P(C|F)P(F)}{P(C)} \\\\  & =\\frac{P(C|F)P(F)}{P(C|{S}_{1})P({S}_{1})+P(C|{S}_{2})P({S}_{2})+P(C|{S}_{3})P({S}_{3})+P(C|{S}_{3})P({S}_{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.08)(0.35)}{(0.12)(0.25)+(0.05)(0.25)+(0.06)(0.25)+(0.03)(0.25)} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.028}{0.065} \\\\  & ≈0.431,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
